From 9522ea8ad0bed3c3fd1b4f570ed9792dec8176d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:21:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] viz: Allow native-handle SharedImages in frame-sink video
 capture

kPreferSharedImageWithNativeHandle already allocates non-CPU-mappable
SCANOUT buffers on Linux (needed for NVIDIA / GBM without LINEAR). The
capturer still only GPU-blits for kPreferMappableSharedImage and CHECKs
that preference on ARGB results.

Treat native-handle like mappable for texture capture, and only mark
BlitRequest as populating a mappable SharedImage when the preference is
actually mappable.

Bug: 428022619
Change-Id: Ia19bf4e65e668c69dd0dad8851bac8f3d27da975
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8220427
Commit-Queue: Ilya Nikolaevskiy <ilnik@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy <ilnik@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Jordan Bayles <jophba@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698105}
